Package: adaptive2in1count
Type: Package
Title: 2-in-1 Adaptive Designs for Overdispersed Count Endpoints
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given  = "Gosuke",
    family = "Homma",
    role   = c("aut", "cre"),
    email  = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com"
  )
Description: Evaluates the operating characteristics of a two-group 2-in-1
    adaptive design whose Phase 2 and Phase 3 parts use overdispersed count
    endpoints, such as the exacerbation count over a short window and the
    annualized exacerbation rate in asthma and chronic obstructive pulmonary
    disease. Counts follow an additive gamma frailty model, so each endpoint is
    marginally negative binomial with its own dispersion, and the two endpoints
    of a patient are correlated both through the frailty and through the
    follow-up period they share. Patients may leave before the end of that
    period, with the period distributed as in Tang (2015)
    <doi:10.1080/10543406.2014.971167>. Final analyses are Wald tests of the log
    rate ratio from a negative binomial model with an offset for the realized
    exposure, and the type I error rate, the power, the probability of
    expansion, the expected sample size and the required sample size follow from
    the resulting trivariate normal distribution. Simulation and an exact
    evaluation under complete follow-up are provided for checking. The design
    follows the 2-in-1 framework of Chen, Anderson, Mehrotra, Rubin and Tse
    (2018) <doi:10.1016/j.cct.2017.09.006>.
